The suite's patch for BC-250 Mesh Shaders, applied on top of the DirectMesh v1.3.1 patch for Mesa 26.2.1.

RADV_BC250_MESH_SPLIT_WRITES (default off, per game): a split Mesh shader may store to buffers (SSBO and
global), and may use an external atomic's result when that result only decides other such writes, as the
fault reporting of PS5 emulators does (a compare-exchange whose result gates the stores of a fault record).
The writes run in the first piece only, exactly once per original workgroup; the other pieces see the
atomic's result as zero and keep nothing that depends on it. Memory fences without an execution scope stay
in every piece. The switch declares that the shader never reads those writes back: that cannot be proven
from the shader, so the refusals of storage reads are lifted under it.

